type: software
title: "Sharp exponential rates for permanent-on-top and anomalous boson bunching at fixed rank"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. At every fixed rank d the worst ratio between the largest eigenvalue of the Schur power of a positive semidefinite matrix and its permanent grows with a sharp exponential base: e/2 at complex rank two, e^2/6 at real rank three, tending to e^gamma. The best general constant c* satisfies e^gamma <= c* <= e^(1+gamma). Balanced permanental compounds and anomalous multimode boson bunching have the same sharp bases."
